1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,344
Your refrigerator has picked up a new hobby: percussion.

2
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:07,706
Let's use SoHelpMe to work through an unfamiliar rattle, one

3
00:00:07,866 --> 00:00:09,422
observation at a time.

4
00:00:09,932 --> 00:00:12,858
I describe the intermittent rattling and mention that the

5
00:00:13,018 --> 00:00:15,084
refrigerator still seems cold.

6
00:00:15,244 --> 00:00:16,835
Plain language is enough.

7
00:00:16,995 --> 00:00:20,513
I don't need to know the name of a single refrigerator part.

8
00:00:21,023 --> 00:00:22,462
Now I choose Get help.

9
00:00:22,622 --> 00:00:27,116
SoHelpMe responds with a practical first check and asks for more

10
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:31,954
information, instead of expecting me to arrive with a diagnosis.

11
00:00:32,464 --> 00:00:36,075
Here, the response points to items that may be touching or

12
00:00:36,235 --> 00:00:38,998
vibrating, and asks what changes the rattle.

13
00:00:39,158 --> 00:00:42,746
I can read the suggestion and answer what I actually notice.

14
00:00:43,256 --> 00:00:47,528
For this demonstration, I report that two glass bottles were

15
00:00:47,688 --> 00:00:49,163
touching inside the door.

16
00:00:49,323 --> 00:00:53,200
Separating them stopped the rattle, and the refrigerator is still

17
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,312
cooling normally.

18
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:58,387
The follow-up recommends keeping the bottles apart and monitoring

19
00:00:58,547 --> 00:01:00,033
whether the sound returns.

20
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:04,349
That's a useful next step for this example, with room to continue if

21
00:01:04,509 --> 00:01:05,891
the problem changes.

22
00:01:06,401 --> 00:01:10,801
A clearer description, a useful question, and a practical next step.

23
00:01:10,961 --> 00:01:11,924
SoHelpMe.

24
00:01:12,084 --> 00:01:13,733
A little help when you need it.
